{title: The Great Physician}
{artist: William Hunter / John H. Stockton}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Three (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing, 1950), # 145)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]The great Physician now is near,
[D]The sympathizing [A7]Je[D]sus;
[D]He speaks the drooping heart to cheer,
[D]Oh! hear the voice of [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A7]Sweetest [D]note in [G]seraph [D]song,
[A7]Sweetest [D]name on [G]mortal [D]tongue;
[D]Sweetest carol ever sung,
[D]Jesus, blessèd [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Your many sins are all forgiv’n,
[D]Oh! hear the voice of [A7]Je[D]sus;
[D]Go on your way in peace to Heav’n,
[D]And wear a crown with [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]All glory to the dying Lamb!
[D]I now believe in [A7]Je[D]sus;
[D]I love the blessèd Savior’s name,
[D]I love the name of [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]The children, too, both great and small,
[D]Who love the name of [A7]Je[D]sus,
[D]May now accept the gracious call
[D]To work and live for [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Come, brethren, help me sing His praise,
[D]Oh, praise the name of [A7]Je[D]sus;
[D]Oh, sisters, all your voices raise,
[D]Oh, bless the name of [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]His name dispels my guilt and fear,
[D]No other name but [A7]Je[D]sus;
[D]Oh! how my soul delights to hear
[D]The charming name of [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[D]And when to that bright world above,
[D]We rise to see our [A7]Je[D]sus,
[D]We’ll sing around the throne of love
[D]His name, the name of [A7]Je[D]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
